{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And what the land is that he dwells in — and 'what the land' that we said above speaks of the land that is at the edge of the kingdom, where there is no settlement; but now it speaks of the land that they dwell in." "Whether it is good or bad — whether it is full of abundant produce and they will find in it everything good for their wars, so that they will not need to prepare provisions for themselves so extensively in advance, at the time of war beforehand." "In camps — dwelling, or in fortified cities. All this is to know whether they need to build siege-works and ramps to conquer the cities."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:09.284522624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}